Brief reasoning:
The mutagenized element is the *SORT1* liver enhancer (chr1p13.3) assayed in HepG2 cells, containing the active C/EBP binding site around positions 393–403 (the rs12740374 region) as well as functional GC-box/SP1/KLF motifs (positions 204–220, 365–380), an ETS/purine-rich regulatory module (positions 270–295), and flanking CCAAT/C/EBP-like and HNF motifs (positions 318–340, 440–455). Variants disrupting these activator binding sites—most notably the core C/EBP motif at positions 395–403 and the purine-rich activator cluster at 272–291—produce substantial decreases in reporter activity, whereas peripheral variants outside conserved motifs have near-neutral effects.

